BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Our Little Secret Book Launch
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260519T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260519T190000
UID:bm-5169020260519@shop.benmcnallybooks.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/7600763/Website2/
 Events/2026_Our_Little_Secret.png?cb=1777151470
DESCRIPTION:[at Ben McNally Books]\nJoin us at Ben McNally Books\, in part
 nership with Cormorant Books\, to celebrate the launch of\nOur Little Secr
 et\n\, by Edward Kay and Mikhael Klassen-Kay.\nOrder a Copy of the book h
 ere.\nAbout the Book\nTwelfth-grade English teacher Mr. Lowell turns up de
 ad one May morning. Cause of death: autoerotic asphyxiation gone wrong. Ev
 eryone at Ridgeview Alternative School is shocked. Everyone\, that is\, ex
 cept honor students Jordan Byrne\, Nick Moretti\, and Chloe Underwood.\nBa
 ck in September\, aspiring civil rights lawyer Jordan\, Juilliard-hopeful 
 Nick\, and budding actress Chloe land in Clifford “Call Me Cliff” Lowe
 ll’s classroom with big dreams of university scholarships and lucrative 
 careers. Soon\, they discover the well-respected educator and head of the 
 Teachers’ Federation is actually a sexual predator with a long list of v
 ictims — a list that’s about to include the three of them. Facing a ma
 nipulative monster\, a complacent administration\, and grim futures\, the 
 trio hatches a desperate plot: plan a murder so perfect that maybe\, just 
 maybe\, they can get away with it …\nAbout the Author\nEdward Kay is an 
 award-winning author and screenwriter with eight published books and more 
 than 130 hours of produced television for broadcasters including BBC\, Dis
 ney\, CBC\, France Télévisions\, ABC Australia\, and Bell Media.\nMikhae
 l Klassen-Kay is a Toronto-based author with an Honours Bachelor of Arts f
 rom the University of Toronto. A fan of historical memoirs and Gothic fict
 ion\, his work explores themes of queerness and neurodiversity through a d
 arkly comedic lens.
LOCATION:Ben McNally Books
URL:https://shop.benmcnallybooks.com/events
X-SOURCE:Ben McNally Books
END:VEVENT
